---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'September 14, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — SVGWire"
  description="SVGWire Terms of Service. Simple, clear terms governing the use of SVGWire's free client-side SVG conversion and sprite generation tools."
  canonical="https://svgwire.com/terms"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[860px] px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
      <p class="text-caption-mono text-mute uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-body-sm text-mute">Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <div class="space-y-10 text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
      <!-- 1. Acceptance of Terms -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using the SVGWire website located at <a href="https://svgwire.com" class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">https://svgwire.com</a> ("Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, please do not use the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Description of Service -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">2. Description of Service</h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire provides a free, browser-based web utility that transforms SVG (Scalable Vector Graphics) assets into frontend component code (including React, Vue 3, Svelte 5, React Native, and Tailwind CSS formats), compiles SVG sprite sheets, and converts folders of SVG files in bulk.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          All core file processing, code compilation, and archive compression take place locally in your web browser.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Acceptable Use -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">3. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to use the Service only for lawful purposes. You must not:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>Attempt to interfere with, disrupt, or compromise the integrity or security of the Service infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Use automated scripts or bots to spam, overload, or maliciously attack the website.</li>
          <li>Use the Service to process or distribute content that is illegal, harmful, or infringes on the intellectual property rights of third parties.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. User Responsibility for Content -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">4. User Responsibility for Content</h2>
        <p>
          You are solely responsible for all SVG files, code, and content that you input into SVGWire or export using the Service. You represent and warrant that you possess all necessary rights, licenses, and permissions to use and convert the SVG assets you supply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Intellectual Property -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">5. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire and its original branding, website design, UI layout, logos, source code, and assets are owned by [INSERT LEGAL ENTITY / COMPANY NAME] and are protected by applicable copyright, trademark, and intellectual property laws.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          SVGWire claims no copyright or ownership interest in the SVG files you input or the converted component code generated from your inputs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Third-Party SVG Assets and Trademarks -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">6. Third-Party Assets and Trademarks</h2>
        <p>
          Framework names and product trademarks referenced on SVGWire (such as React, Vue, Svelte, React Native, Tailwind CSS, Cloudflare, and Figma) belong to their respective trademark holders. Reference to these trademarks does not imply affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement by those entity owners.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Generated Code & Output -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">7. Generated Code & Output</h2>
        <p>
          Code generated by SVGWire is provided "as is". You are granted full permission to copy, modify, integrate, and distribute the generated code in both non-commercial and commercial software applications without attribution to SVGWire.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Service Availability -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">8. Service Availability</h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. We reserve the right to modify, suspend, or discontinue any aspect of the Service at any time without prior notice or liability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. Disclaimer of Warranties -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">9. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE GENERATED CODE WILL BE ERROR-FREE OR UNINTERRUPTED.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. Limitation of Liability -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          IN NO EVENT SHALL SVGWIRE, ITS OPERATORS, OR CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR USE, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH YOUR USE OR INABILITY TO USE THE SERVICE OR GENERATED CODE.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Changes to Service and Terms -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">11. Changes to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to revise these Terms of Service at any time. Modified terms will become effective immediately upon posting to this page. Your continued use of the Service following any changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 12. Governing Law -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">12. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of [INSERT JURISDICTION / GOVERNING LAW], without regard to its conflict of law provisions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 13. Contact Information -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">13. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          For any legal inquiries or questions regarding these Terms of Service, please contact:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-4 font-mono text-body-sm">
          <p>Entity: [INSERT LEGAL ENTITY / COMPANY NAME]</p>
          <p>Email: [INSERT CONTACT EMAIL ADDRESS]</p>
          <p>Website: https://svgwire.com</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
